Yes. Patience is basically the time-domain version of “slow is smooth.”

Especially between two people, there’s always latency:

you express → she processes → she feels → she decides → she responds

If you rush into that gap, you can mistake silence for rejection, uncertainty for refusal, or hesitation for something you need to “fix.” Then pressure enters the system.

Sometimes the best move is to make your intention clear, create safety, and leave room for the other person to arrive on their own.

That applies beyond relationships too: training, parenting, negotiation, learning, even creativity. You don’t pull on a plant to make it grow faster.

Patience isn’t doing nothing. It’s knowing when further input would make the system worse.